 Democrat Jon Ossoff against Republican Mike Collins. Polling throughout the fall has been remarkably consistent: every poll since mid-August shows Ossoff ahead, with margins ranging from four to ten points, including surveys from Republican-leaning firms like Trafalgar, Rasmussen, and InsiderAdvantage. Averages put Ossoff up roughly eight to nine points.\n\nOssoff holds a decisive financial edge, with $42.6 million on hand compared to Collins' $2.1 million, though outside groups have spent modestly against both. Expert raters overwhelmingly call the race Likely D or better, and prediction markets price Ossoff's chances at 94 to 97 percent. The first debate in early October was heated but produced no clear sign of a shift. The race remains Ossoff's to lose.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9355, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9397, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9457, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9522, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9495, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9478, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9479, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9545, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.928, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9516, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9505, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9677, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9512, "margin": 9.0}]}